  "goodToKnow": "Die Vollbeschäftigung is full employment, when practically everyone who wants a job has one. West Germany reached it during the Wirtschaftswunder of the late 1950s and 60s, recruiting Gastarbeiter from Italy, Turkey and elsewhere to fill gaps. Some southern German regions today have unemployment rates near full employment. For a full-time job, say eine Vollzeitstelle. It has no plural."
